---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBand from '../../components/layout/ContactBand.astro';
import { groceryOptions } from '../../data/grocery-demo';
import { projects } from '../../data/projects';

const codeExcerpts = ["STORE_QUERY_GROUPS = {\n  \"Walmart\": [\"Walmart\", \"Walmart Grocery\"],\n  \"Independent\": [\"Your Independent Grocer\"],\n}\n\nresponse = requests.get(\n  FLIPP_SEARCH_URL, params=params,\n  headers=headers, timeout=timeout_seconds\n)", "response = client.models.generate_content(\n  model=model_name,\n  contents=prompt,\n  config=types.GenerateContentConfig(\n    response_mime_type=\"application/json\"\n  ),\n)\npayload = json.loads(response.text)", "df = df.drop_duplicates(\n  subset=[\"Store\", \"Product\", \"Sale Price\"]\n).reset_index(drop=True)"];

const project = projects.find((item) => item.slug === 'grocery-automation');
if (!project) throw new Error('Grocery Automation project data is unavailable.');
---
<BaseLayout title={project.title} description={project.premise} canonicalPath={project.route}>
  <article class="grocery-case">
    <header class="grocery-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 · Automation</p>
      <p class="grocery-meta">Python · structured flyer data · Gemini · JSON · Excel</p>
      <h1>Grocery Automation</h1>
      <p class="grocery-lede">A recurring planning task became a repeatable pipeline: flyer data in, rule-constrained menu options and a reviewable Excel output out.</p>
      <p class="grocery-authorship">I designed and implemented the workflow with AI-assisted coding support, defining the rules, testing each version, and changing the architecture when the real workflow exposed a weak point.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="grocery-section grocery-pipeline" aria-labelledby="pipeline-title">
      <div class="grocery-heading"><p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p><h2 id="pipeline-title">A practical pipeline, not a one-step prompt</h2></div>
      <ol class="grocery-pipeline-list">
        <li>Flyer data</li><li>Python extraction</li><li>Product records</li><li>Gemini + rules</li><li>JSON</li><li>Excel</li><li>Human review</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="grocery-reading"><p>The system was built for a recurring group meal-planning job: review sale information, plan varied dinners for a group, respect restrictions and pantry assumptions, and produce an orderable comparison another person could read. Gemini was one stage in a wider workflow, not the whole product.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="grocery-section" aria-labelledby="pivot-title">
      <div class="grocery-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Decision one</p><h2 id="pivot-title">When browser automation became brittle, change the representation</h2></div>
      <div class="grocery-reading"><p>I began with browser automation. It could reach the retailer site, but bot protection made the visible frontend a poor dependency. Rather than trying to force that route, I moved to Flipp and then to the structured Wishabi/Flipp JSON data used behind the flyer experience.</p><p>That pivot turned a screen-reading problem into a product-and-price record problem. Python could request the structured results, keep only the fields needed downstream, and pass a compact product table to the planning stage.</p></div>
      <pre class="grocery-code" aria-label="Approved code excerpt showing the final store query groups"><code>{codeExcerpts[0]}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="grocery-section" aria-labelledby="rules-title">
      <div class="grocery-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Decision two</p><h2 id="rules-title">Put the human rules in the system</h2></div>
      <div class="grocery-rule-grid">
        <div><h3>Scale</h3><p>Exactly 6 dinners for 9 adult portions.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Preferences</h3><p>Chicken thighs, ground beef, tacos, smash burgers, Greek and Mexican flavours.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Constraints</h3><p>Pork-free and shellfish-free; avoid premium proteins chosen only because they are on sale.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Pantry</h3><p>Basic oil, seasonings, salt, pepper, oregano, and garlic powder were already available.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="grocery-reading"><p>The useful behaviour did not come from asking a model to “make a menu.” The script made portions, exclusions, preferred meals, available pantry items, and protein-reuse logic explicit. The model could interpret the product data within those bounds, while a person still reviewed the result.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="grocery-section" aria-labelledby="json-title">
      <div class="grocery-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Decision three</p><h2 id="json-title">Prose was readable. JSON was usable.</h2></div>
      <div class="grocery-reading"><p>The first model integration returned a long block of prose. A person could read it, but Python could not reliably turn it into a spreadsheet. I updated the SDK integration after it changed, then required a nested JSON response with separate store options, days, meals, ingredients, instructions, and costs.</p><p>That made the AI output a component in a larger system: Python could validate the expected shape before generating the workbook, instead of treating a fluent paragraph as the endpoint.</p></div>
      <pre class="grocery-code" aria-label="Approved code excerpt showing structured JSON output"><code>{codeExcerpts[1]}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="grocery-section" aria-labelledby="store-title">
      <div class="grocery-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Decision four</p><h2 id="store-title">Retailer quirks belonged in the data layer</h2></div>
      <div class="grocery-reading"><p>A single Walmart search sometimes surfaced general merchandise while missing useful grocery sale items. I added a second Walmart Grocery query, normalized both searches under Walmart, and removed overlapping rows. The public version also includes the store in its deduplication key so identical items at different stores remain separate. This was a small change with a practical effect: the comparison better reflected what someone could actually see in the flyer.</p></div>
      <pre class="grocery-code" aria-label="Approved code excerpt showing store-aware deduplication"><code>{codeExcerpts[2]}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="grocery-section grocery-sample" aria-labelledby="sample-title">
      <div class="grocery-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Sample output</p><h2 id="sample-title">Two six-dinner options, ready for review</h2></div>
      <p class="grocery-sample-label">SAMPLE / DEMONSTRATION DATA — NOT LIVE PRICES</p>
      <div class="grocery-reading"><p>These two options come from the approved deterministic demonstration response. Every option is scaled for 9 portions and lists six dinners. The totals are meal-level demo totals; they are comparison aids, not current baskets or an optimization result.</p></div>
      <div class="grocery-table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Sample six-dinner options by store. Scroll horizontally if needed.">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Dinner</th>{groceryOptions.map((option) => <th scope="col">{option.store}</th>)}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>{Array.from({ length: 6 }, (_, index) => <tr><th scope="row">Day {index + 1}</th>{groceryOptions.map((option) => <td>{option.meals[index]}<small class="meal-cost">{option.costs[index]}</small></td>)}</tr>)}</tbody>
          <tfoot><tr><th scope="row">Demo total</th>{groceryOptions.map((option) => <td>{option.total}</td>)}</tr></tfoot>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="grocery-details-grid">
        {groceryOptions.map((option) => (
          <details class="grocery-details">
            <summary>{option.store} sample ingredient detail</summary>
            <p><strong>{option.spotlight.meal}</strong><br />{option.spotlight.instructions}</p>
            <div class="grocery-table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label={`${option.store} sample ingredient details. Scroll horizontally if needed.`}>
              <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Ingredient</th><th scope="col">Size</th><th scope="col">Units</th><th scope="col">Sample total</th></tr></thead><tbody>{option.spotlight.ingredients.map((ingredient) => <tr><th scope="row">{ingredient.item}</th><td>{ingredient.size}</td><td>{ingredient.units}</td><td>{ingredient.total}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="grocery-caveat">Some components are marked <em>estimate</em> when they were not present in the flyer data. Those are model estimates, not live shelf prices.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="grocery-section grocery-close" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
      <div class="grocery-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Limits and next steps</p><h2 id="limits-title">Useful automation still needs a person</h2></div>
      <div class="grocery-reading"><p>I used and refined the workflow in practice, especially as retailer behaviour and workbook readability surfaced edge cases. It is not a procurement platform: Flipp/Wishabi is a third-party dependency, the data shape can change, and a human should review the final plan. Missing non-sale prices may be estimated, so the system does not claim a single best basket or place an order.</p><p>Next, I would add a current source for non-sale prices, separate configuration from implementation more cleanly, and keep the deterministic demo mode so the workflow remains explainable even when outside services are unavailable.</p></div>
    </section>
  </article>
  <ContactBand />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .grocery-case { max-width: var(--content-main); margin-inline: auto; padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem) clamp(1.125rem, 3vw, 2.25rem) clamp(4.5rem, 8vw, 7rem); }
  .grocery-hero { max-width: 67rem; padding-bottom: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .grocery-meta { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 760; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .grocery-hero h1 { margin: 0; max-width: 51rem; font-size: clamp(3.25rem, 7vw, 6.3rem); line-height: .96; letter-spacing: -.06em; }
  .grocery-lede { max-width: 46rem; margin: 1.65rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text); font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.65vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.55; }
  .grocery-authorship { max-width: 45rem; margin: 1.1rem 0 0; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .92rem; }
  .grocery-section { padding-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem); }
  .grocery-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: 2rem; align-items: start; }
  .grocery-heading .eyebrow { margin: .5rem 0 0; }
  .grocery-heading h2 { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.6vw, 4.3rem); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.052em; }
  .grocery-reading { max-width: var(--content-reading); margin: 1.75rem 0 0 auto; color: var(--color-text); }
  .grocery-reading p { margin: 0; font-size: 1.04rem; }
  .grocery-reading p + p { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .grocery-pipeline-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .7rem .95rem; margin: 1.9rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .grocery-pipeline-list li { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .95rem; color: var(--color-ink); font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 780; }
  .grocery-pipeline-list li:not(:last-child)::after { content: '→'; color: var(--color-teal); }
  .grocery-code { max-width: var(--content-reading); margin: 1.5rem 0 0 auto; padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem; overflow-x: auto; border-left: .25rem solid var(--color-teal); background: #e9f0ee; color: #1d3635; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: .81rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .meal-cost { display: block; margin-top: .4rem; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .grocery-code code { font: inherit; }
  .grocery-rule-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1px; margin-top: 1.9rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-line); background: var(--color-line); }
  .grocery-rule-grid > div { padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem; background: var(--color-surface); }
  .grocery-rule-grid h3 { margin: 0; color: var(--color-teal); font-size: 1rem; }
  .grocery-rule-grid p { margin: .45rem 0 0; color: var(--color-text); font-size: .91rem; }
  .grocery-sample-label { display: inline-block; margin: 1.8rem 0 0; padding: .5rem .7rem; background: var(--color-pale-teal); color: var(--color-deep-teal); font-size: .76rem; font-weight: 820; letter-spacing: .06em; }
  .grocery-table-wrap { max-width: 100%; margin-top: 1.5rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--color-line); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .grocery-table-wrap:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--color-focus); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .grocery-table-wrap table { width: 100%; min-width: 44rem; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left; }
  .grocery-table-wrap th, .grocery-table-wrap td { padding: .85rem .9rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); vertical-align: top; font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .grocery-table-wrap th { color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 800; }
  .grocery-table-wrap thead th { background: var(--color-deep-teal); color: white; }
  .grocery-table-wrap tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: #f7faf9; }
  .grocery-table-wrap tfoot { background: var(--color-surface-soft); }
  .grocery-details-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .grocery-details { border: 1px solid var(--color-line); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .grocery-details summary { min-height: 2.75rem; padding: .9rem 1rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--color-ink); font-size: .92rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .grocery-details summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--color-focus); outline-offset: -3px; }
  .grocery-details p { margin: 0; padding: 0 1rem; color: var(--color-text); font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .grocery-details .grocery-table-wrap { margin: 1rem; max-width: calc(100% - 2rem); }
  .grocery-details .grocery-table-wrap table { min-width: 29rem; }
  .grocery-caveat { max-width: var(--content-reading); margin: 1.1rem 0 0 auto; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .83rem; }
  .grocery-close { padding-bottom: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 51.25rem) { .grocery-heading { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .grocery-heading .eyebrow { margin: 0; } .grocery-reading { margin-left: 0; } }
  @media (max-width: 35rem) { .grocery-case { padding-inline: 1.125rem; } .grocery-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(3.1rem, 15vw, 4.3rem); } .grocery-rule-grid, .grocery-details-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .grocery-details, .grocery-details * { transition-duration: .001ms !important; animation-duration: .001ms !important; } }
</style>
